  "description": "HAJGUY crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group I 2 2 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C32 H66 Dy9 N8 O58 1+,H1 O1 1-,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy1C (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2C (Dy) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.575-5.118 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.05-167.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy9(μ4-OH)2(μ3-OH)8(μ2-OCH3)4(NO3)8(H2O)8(L)4](OH)·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
